{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1334 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "17821ce4715c9b7e836f036d421d96c7f2fe58fa48dcc705b5ce3105a37979ce" :edb/db-before-t 1333 :edb/db-after-t 1334 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534646 50 #inst "2026-10-08T03:08:07.631Z" 13194139534646 true] [17592186087487 1100 "Calculate the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola $\\dfrac{(x+1)^2}{10} - \\dfrac{y^2}{25} = 1$." 13194139534646 false] [17592186087487 1100 "Calculate the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola $\\dfrac{(x+1)^2}{10} - \\dfrac{y^2}{25} = 1.$" 13194139534646 true] [17592186087487 1145 "To find the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n((x + 1)^{2})/(10) - \\frac{y^{2}}{25} &= 1 \\\\\n((x + 1)^{2})/(10) - \\frac{0^{2}}{25} &= 1 \\\\\n((x + 1)^{2})/(10) &= 1 \\\\\n(x + 1)^{2} &= 10 \\\\\nx + 1 &= ± \\sqrt{10} \\\\\nx &= -1 ± \\sqrt{10}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercepts are\n\n$$\n\\left(-1\\pm \\sqrt{10},0\\right)\n$$" 13194139534646 false] [17592186087487 1145 "To find the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{10}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{10}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{10} & =1 \\\\ (x+1)^{2} & =10 \\\\ x+1 & =\\pm \\sqrt{10} \\\\ x & =-1\\pm \\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercepts are $\\left(-1\\pm \\sqrt{10},0\\right).$" 13194139534646 true] [17592186087488 1100 "Calculate the points where the hyperbola\n$\\dfrac{x^2}{10}-\\dfrac{y^2}{15}=1$\nintersects the line $y=-3$." 13194139534646 false] [17592186087488 1100 "Calculate the points where the hyperbola \n$\\dfrac{x^2}{10}-\\dfrac{y^2}{15}=1$\nintersects the line $y=-3.$" 13194139534646 true] [17592186087488 1145 "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=-3$, we substitute $y=-3$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{x^{2}}{10} - \\frac{y^{2}}{15} &= 1 \\\\\n\\frac{x^{2}}{10} - ((-3)^{2})/(15) &= 1 \\\\\n\\frac{x^{2}}{10} - \\frac{9}{15} &= 1 \\\\\n\\frac{x^{2}}{10} - \\frac{3}{5} &= 1 \\\\\nx^{2} - 6 &= 10 \\\\\nx^{2} &= 16 \\\\\nx &= ± 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the hyperbola intersects the horizontal line $y=-3$ at the points $(\\pm 4, -3)$." 13194139534646 false] [17592186087488 1145 "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=-3,$ we substitute $y=-3$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{10}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{15} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{10}-\\frac{(-3)^{2}}{15} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{10}-\\frac{9}{15} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{10}-\\frac{3}{5} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}-6 & =10 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =16 \\\\ x & =\\pm 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the hyperbola intersects the horizontal line $y=-3$ at the points $(\\pm 4, -3).$" 13194139534646 true] [17592186087564 1100 "Calculate the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola $7y^2 -5x^2 = 28$." 13194139534646 false] [17592186087564 1100 "Calculate the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola $7y^2 -5x^2 = 28.$" 13194139534646 true] [17592186087564 1145 "To find the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n7y^{2} - 5x^{2} &= 28 \\\\\n7y^{2} - 5(0)^{2} &= 28 \\\\\n7y^{2} &= 28 \\\\\ny^{2} &= 4 \\\\\ny &= ± 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercepts are $(0,\\pm 2)$." 13194139534646 false] [17592186087564 1145 "To find the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7{y}^{2}-5{x}^{2} & =28 \\\\ 7{y}^{2}-5(0)^{2} & =28 \\\\ 7{y}^{2} & =28 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4 \\\\ y & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercepts are $(0,\\pm 2).$" 13194139534646 true] [17592186087565 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038690/assets/c8d69cebc1c7388bb9bc8ac73152a9b2941156188917ee6b680f6758a3d777de.png)\n\nCalculate the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $\\dfrac{x^2}{9} - \\dfrac{y^2}{25}=1$ intersects the line $y = x.$" 13194139534646 true] [17592186087565 1100 "Calculate the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $\\dfrac{x^2}{9} - \\dfrac{y^2}{25}=1$ intersects the line $y = x$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/874/Source/Images/39c8aedbe6ab698c5a77db42509d3ef3.png)" 13194139534646 false] [17592186087565 1145 "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=x$, we first replace $y$ with $x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{x^{2}}{9} - \\frac{y^{2}}{25} &= 1 \\\\\n\\frac{x^{2}}{9} - \\frac{x^{2}}{25} &= 1 \\\\\n\\frac{16x^{2}}{225} &= 1 \\\\\nx^{2} &= \\frac{225}{16} \\\\\nx &= ± \\frac{15}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534646 false] [17592186087565 1145 "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=x,$ we first replace $y$ with $x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{16{x}^{2}}{225} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =\\frac{225}{16} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\frac{15}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534646 true] [17592186087774 1020 #edb/ref 17592186301116 13194139534646 true] [17592186087774 1020 #edb/ref 17592186301157 13194139534646 true] [17592186087774 1020 #edb/ref 17592186301164 13194139534646 true] [17592186087774 1020 #edb/ref 17592186301178 13194139534646 true] [17592186087774 1020 #edb/ref 17592186301185 13194139534646 true] [17592186087775 1020 #edb/ref 17592186301125 13194139534646 true] [17592186087775 1020 #edb/ref 17592186301192 13194139534646 true] [17592186087775 1020 #edb/ref 17592186301199 13194139534646 true] [17592186087776 1020 #edb/ref 17592186301109 13194139534646 true] [17592186087776 1020 #edb/ref 17592186301135 13194139534646 true] [17592186087776 1020 #edb/ref 17592186301152 13194139534646 true] [17592186087776 1020 #edb/ref 17592186301171 13194139534646 true] [17592186087777 1020 #edb/ref 17592186301102 13194139534646 true] [17592186087777 1020 #edb/ref 17592186301141 13194139534646 true] [17592186087777 1020 #edb/ref 17592186301147 13194139534646 true] [17592186087990 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534646 true] [17592186087990 1100 "Calculate the points where the hyperbola $\\frac{x^{2}}{4} - \\frac{y^{2}}{9} = 1$ intersects the line $x =-1$." 13194139534646 false] [17592186087990 1100 "Calculate the points where the hyperbola $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1$ intersects the line $x=-1.$" 13194139534646 true] [17592186087990 1145 "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $x=-1,$ we substitute $x=-1$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(-1)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ -\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-\\frac{27}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe cannot take the square root of a negative number. Therefore, the equation has no real solutions. \nSo, the hyperbola does not intersect the vertical line $x=-1.$" 13194139534646 true] [17592186088369 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534646 true] [17592186088369 1100 "Calculate the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola $((x - 2)^{2})/(5) - ((y + 4)^{2})/(16) = 1$." 13194139534646 false] [17592186088369 1100 "Calculate the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola $\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{5}-\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{16}=1.$" 13194139534646 true] [17592186088369 1145 "To find the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{5}-\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(0-2)^{2}}{5}-\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}-\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ -\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{16} & =1-\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{16} & =\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ (y+4)^{2} & =-\\frac{16}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe cannot take the square root of a negative number. Therefore, the equation has no real solutions. So, there are no $y$-intercepts." 13194139534646 true] [17592186301102 1017 #edb/ref 17592186301103 13194139534646 true] [17592186301102 1089 "q-10485" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301102 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534646 true] [17592186301102 1100 "Calculate the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}=1$ intersects the line $y=x.$" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301102 1113 #uuid "296c1691-3fdb-50aa-926f-7c3fb307cb51" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301102 1145 "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=x,$ we first replace $y$ with $x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}}{36}-\\frac{9{x}^{2}}{36} & =1 \\\\ -\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{36} & =1 \\\\ 5{x}^{2} & =-36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe cannot take the square root of a negative number. Therefore, the equation has no real solutions. So, the hyperbola does not intersect the line $y=x.$" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301103 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301104 13194139534646 true] [17592186301103 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301105 13194139534646 true] [17592186301103 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301106 13194139534646 true] [17592186301103 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301107 13194139534646 true] [17592186301103 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301108 13194139534646 true] [17592186301103 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534646 true] [17592186301103 1041 "selection" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301103 1104 #edb/ref 17592186301106 13194139534646 true] [17592186301103 1110 #uuid "b43c252e-1e90-5658-9203-1fa02a327d3a" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301104 1034 "x=\\pm 2" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301104 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534646 true] [17592186301104 1111 #uuid "8672317d-3771-5265-a89f-7b6f8e99ade1" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301105 1034 "x=\\pm 4" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301105 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534646 true] [17592186301105 1111 #uuid "12acd7b8-4127-59f1-9e73-40f94e478f08" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301106 1034 "There are no points of intersection" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301106 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534646 true] [17592186301106 1111 #uuid "d03d5fc6-c23f-5bfa-ac8b-43425dfe8f01" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301107 1034 "x=\\pm 9" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301107 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534646 true] [17592186301107 1111 #uuid "95ca5daa-819d-5de2-a607-2a15fd38eaee" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301108 1034 "x=\\pm 3" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301108 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534646 true] [17592186301108 1111 #uuid "5b70dbea-e3cb-5626-94fc-d756d225180b" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301109 1017 #edb/ref 17592186301110 13194139534646 true] [17592186301109 1089 "q-10495" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301109 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534646 true] [17592186301109 1100 "Calculate the points where the hyperbola $9{y}^{2}-20{x}^{2}=180$ intersects the line $x=6.$" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301109 1113 #uuid "63269d3f-c004-594d-a48d-9275a75ead43" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301109 1145 "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $x=6,$ we substitute $x=6$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{y}^{2}-20{x}^{2} & =180 \\\\ 9{y}^{2}-20(6)^{2} & =180 \\\\ 9{y}^{2}-720 & =180 \\\\ {y}^{2}-80 & =20 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =80+20 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =100 \\\\ y & =\\pm 10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the hyperbola intersects the vertical line $x=6$  at the points $(6,\\pm 10).$" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301110 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301111 13194139534646 true] [17592186301110 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301112 13194139534646 true] [17592186301110 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301113 13194139534646 true] [17592186301110 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301114 13194139534646 true] [17592186301110 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301115 13194139534646 true] [17592186301110 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534646 true] [17592186301110 1041 "selection" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301110 1104 #edb/ref 17592186301111 13194139534646 true] [17592186301110 1110 #uuid "dc039807-37d5-5024-9e5a-319d42aa4df7" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301111 1034 "(6,\\pm 10)" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301111 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534646 true] [17592186301111 1111 #uuid "75cb1614-3d0e-5416-ae62-d7211445e31e" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301112 1034 "(6,\\pm 15)" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301112 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534646 true] [17592186301112 1111 #uuid "e0c80c91-4d30-5607-979d-060505d8a99f" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301113 1034 "(6,\\pm 20)" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301113 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534646 true] [17592186301113 1111 #uuid "b3a2b41d-88bc-5079-a577-3f2e7db19d9c" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301114 1034 "(6,\\pm 5)" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301114 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534646 true] [17592186301114 1111 #uuid "23e72abf-442d-5a55-b855-835afd2b2299" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301115 1034 "(6,\\pm 25)" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301115 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534646 true] [17592186301115 1111 #uuid "80902677-0605-5e17-bdbd-df604c19310f" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301116 1017 #edb/ref 17592186301117 13194139534646 true] [17592186301116 1017 #edb/ref 17592186301119 13194139534646 true] [17592186301116 1017 #edb/ref 17592186301121 13194139534646 true] [17592186301116 1017 #edb/ref 17592186301123 13194139534646 true] [17592186301116 1089 "q-278354" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301116 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534646 true] [17592186301116 1100 "From **left to right,** the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola $\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{8}-(y+1)^{2}=1$ are\n\n$($\n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}} $)\\,$\nand \n$\\,($\n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}} $).$" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301116 1113 #uuid "9a845c77-5cc9-5372-bd5a-7e8ad7351d56" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301116 1145 "To find the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{8}-(y+1)^{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{8}-(0+1)^{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{8}-1 & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{8} & =2 \\\\ (x+2)^{2} & =16 \\\\ x+2 & =\\pm 4 \\\\ x & =-2\\pm 4 \\\\ x & =-6,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the $x$-intercepts are $(-6,0)$ and $(2,0).$" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301117 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301118 13194139534646 true] [17592186301117 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534646 true] [17592186301117 1041 "field-1" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301117 1104 #edb/ref 17592186301118 13194139534646 true] [17592186301117 1110 #uuid "b63db1f3-ea88-5f07-ab7b-81b50aeefc95" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301118 1034 "-6" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301118 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534646 true] [17592186301118 1111 #uuid "7d5884d7-3204-56bb-a3e1-01e6a5f5ffc0" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301119 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301120 13194139534646 true] [17592186301119 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534646 true] [17592186301119 1041 "field-2" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301119 1104 #edb/ref 17592186301120 13194139534646 true] [17592186301119 1110 #uuid "cfc3a74c-3837-5576-930d-3ba36b981b6e" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301120 1034 "0" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301120 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534646 true] [17592186301120 1111 #uuid "720d944c-b04d-5077-9ade-f1ceffdfbef8" 13194139534646 true] [17592186301121 1000 #edb/ref 1759218